  "verdict": "The dense presented-passage score carries the separation: dropping the four dense columns costs 12.0 points of test AUROC (0.982 \u2192 0.862) and is the only single-group removal that does, while dropping lex_overlap costs 0.0, the two rank features 0.0, the cross-encoder 0.7 and the bm25 presented pair 0.4. The block is narrower than its name: dense_presented and dense_top1 are the same number for every item and dense_rank_log is constant at ln 2, so the all-12 gate really has 10 informative columns and 'without the four dense features' removes one distinct signal. The effect is concentrated in rung 4: without it the confirmatory gate's rung-4 abstain precision falls to 0.907 and the exploratory band's to 0.100. lex_overlap alone reaches test AUROC 0.811, so overlap is not what carries the result inside this feature stack \u2014 although the separate surface audit (audit.json) shows overlap is highly predictive of rung membership on its own, which is a different question."
